<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  All display copy lives here, never inline in Kotlin. Two reasons:

  1. It is the Android convention and the only thing that makes the app
     translatable.
  2. It keeps the repo-wide prose rules checkable in one place. With copy
     inline, a grep over *.kt could not tell a user-facing sentence from a
     code comment, and the two have different rules.

  Strings marked translatable="false" are commands, field labels and format
  templates for the debug screen. They are shown on screen but must not be
  reworded or localised.

  Format arguments are all %n$s. Passing an Int to a %d is fine, but passing a
  Double to one throws IllegalFormatConversionException at runtime, and several
  of these take Double thresholds.
-->
